% test_guard_suspend.glp - Suspension with ground guard on unbound reader
%
% Tests that a goal SUSPENDS (not fails) when:
%   1. Head matching encounters an unbound reader (adds to Si)
%   2. A ground() guard fails because the extracted variable is unbound
%
% This exercises the Si→U merge path in _softFailToNextClause.
% Without the fix, the goal would fail instead of suspending.
%
% NOTE: Only one clause — no fallback [] clause that would mask the bug
% by providing an alternative suspension path through Commit.

exported procedure wait_ground(_?).
wait_ground([data(X)|_]) :- ground(X?) | done.

exported procedure done.
done.
